WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:06.959
As the next day began to dawn, Sister Simplice was busy preparing some medicine for Fantine.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.555
Suddenly she looked up and saw Mayor Madeleine standing in front of her.

3
00:00:11.556 --> 00:00:19.285
His first task upon arriving home had been to send a letter to his banker. Then he had come immediately to the infirmary.

4
00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:23.594
"Oh, you startled me!" said Sister Simplice.

5
00:00:23.595 --> 00:00:29.118
"And something terrible must have happened to you because your hair has turned completely white!"

6
00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:31.033
"What are you talking about?"

7
00:00:31.034 --> 00:00:35.848
Sister Simplice found a mirror and showed the mayor his reflection.

8
00:00:35.849 --> 00:00:40.181
"Imagine that," he said quietly. "How’s Fantine?"

9
00:00:40.182 --> 00:00:47.086
Sister Simplice explained that Fantine had improved because she believed that he had gone to fetch Cosette.

10
00:00:47.087 --> 00:00:51.182
Somehow the nun knew that he hadn’t been to Montfermeil.

11
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:56.613
"What will we tell her when she realizes Cosette is not here?" asked Sister Simplice.

12
00:00:56.614 --> 00:01:00.832
"It would be wrong to lie to her. Are you going to get Cosette soon?"

13
00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:05.177
"Of course, but it’ll take some time. May I see Fantine now?"

14
00:01:05.178 --> 00:01:08.896
The sick young woman opened her eyes when the mayor entered.

15
00:01:08.897 --> 00:01:15.756
"Where is Cosette?" she asked, radiating happiness as she said her daughter’s name.

16
00:01:15.757 --> 00:01:18.388
Just then the doctor entered the room.

17
00:01:18.389 --> 00:01:25.287
"Stay calm, my dear," said the doctor. "Your child is here, but you cannot see her until you’re cured.

18
00:01:25.288 --> 00:01:28.713
The excitement of seeing her will make your illness worse."

19
00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:40.308
"I’m well!" insisted Fantine, trying to sit up. She fell back, coughing against her pillow. "But perhaps you’re right."

20
00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:47.523
After the doctor and Sister Simplice left the room, the mayor sat by her bed, holding her hand.

21
00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:54.444
"Montfermeil is such a pretty place, isn’t it, Mayor Madeleine? And what did you think of the Thenardiers?"

22
00:01:54.445 --> 00:02:01.872
The mayor looked anxiously at Fantine, but before he could say anything, she cried out. "I hear my darling singing!"

23
00:02:01.873 --> 00:02:08.592
A child was playing in the courtyard, the daughter of a servant. It was this little girl whom Fantine heard.

24
00:02:08.593 --> 00:02:13.189
Fantine held her breath and listened with a look of joy on her face.

25
00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:22.854
"It’s my Cosette! Oh, how happy we’ll be! She’ll chase butterflies in the grass, and I’ll teach her the alphabet.

26
00:02:22.855 --> 00:02:25.681
And then when she’s older, she’ll. . ."

27
00:02:25.682 --> 00:02:30.181
A look of horror crossed Fantine’s face as she pointed to something behind the mayor.

28
00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:38.760
"Good grief! What’s the matter, Fantine?" Madeleine turned and there, leaning against the doorway, stood Javert.

29
00:02:38.761 --> 00:02:46.919
Fantine had not seen the policeman since the day he had arrested her, and she was sure he had now come for her.

30
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.022
"Mayor Madeleine, save me!" she screamed.

31
00:02:51.023 --> 00:02:55.832
Jean Valjean, whom Fantine knew as Mayor Madeleine, stood up.

32
00:02:55.833 --> 00:03:03.649
He turned to Fantine and said in his kindest voice, "Calm yourself. It’s not for you that this man comes."

33
00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.641
Then Valjean looked steadily at Javert and said, "I know what you want."

34
00:03:08.642 --> 00:03:10.962
"Hurry up," said Javert.

35
00:03:10.963 --> 00:03:13.736
Fantine looked around in confusion.

36
00:03:13.737 --> 00:03:21.054
There was no one in the room except the mayor and the policeman. Javert must be talking to her, no matter what the mayor said.

37
00:03:21.055 --> 00:03:28.379
Then she saw something so odd, stranger than anything that had appeared to her when she was delirious with fever.

38
00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:33.712
She saw Javert seize the mayor by the collar, and the mayor bow his head.

39
00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.768
"Mayor Madeleine!" shouted Fantine.

40
00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:42.379
Javert burst into a horrid laugh, displaying all his teeth.

41
00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:48.458
"There is no Mayor Madeleine here any longer!"

42
00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:52.850
Valjean did not attempt to loosen Javert’s grip on his collar. "Javert—"

43
00:03:52.851 --> 00:03:55.609
"Call me Monsieur Inspector."

44
00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:59.289
"Monsieur, I would like to say something to you in private."

45
00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.776
"No, speak now."

46
00:04:01.777 --> 00:04:04.222
"It’s a confidential matter, so I’d like—"

47
00:04:04.223 --> 00:04:06.855
"What difference does that make to me?"

48
00:04:06.856 --> 00:04:14.214
Valjean turned his head and said, "Give me three days so I can go for the child of this unfortunate woman and make some arrangements for her!

49
00:04:14.215 --> 00:04:21.365
I’ll pay whatever’s necessary, and you can come with me if you want." He said all this as quickly and quietly as possible.

50
00:04:21.366 --> 00:04:27.452
"Are you making fun of me?" asked Javert. "You tell me you’re going to get this woman’s child?

51
00:04:27.453 --> 00:04:33.444
You might as well come right out and ask me for three days to escape. Ha-ha! That’s a good one!"

52
00:04:33.445 --> 00:04:43.357
"Going for my child?" Fantine shivered. "Do you mean she’s not here? Where is Cosette? Monsieur Mayor!"

53
00:04:43.358 --> 00:04:52.412
Javert stamped his foot. "Be quiet! What kind of country is this where convicts are mayors and common criminals are nursed like countesses?

54
00:04:52.413 --> 00:04:56.095
I tell you again there’s no Monsieur Mayor here.

55
00:04:56.096 --> 00:05:04.334
There is a robber, a lawbreaker, a convict named Jean Valjean, and I’ve got him! That’s what there is!"

56
00:05:04.335 --> 00:05:08.780
Fantine started to sit up. She looked at Valjean, then at Javert.

57
00:05:08.781 --> 00:05:15.152
She opened her mouth as if to speak, and then suddenly sank back upon the pillow with her eyes closed.

58
00:05:15.153 --> 00:05:21.238
Valjean put his hand over Javert’s and pulled the policeman’s fingers from his collar.

59
00:05:21.239 --> 00:05:29.818
He quickly checked Fantine’s pulse and then whirled back toward Javert. "You have killed this woman!"

60
00:05:29.819 --> 00:05:35.961
"I don’t have time for this. Come along now before I call the guard downstairs and have him handcuff you."

61
00:05:35.962 --> 00:05:39.821
In the corner of the room there was an old bed with a metal frame.

62
00:05:39.822 --> 00:05:43.723
It was where the nuns rested when they had to watch over a patient at night.

63
00:05:43.724 --> 00:05:51.207
Valjean rushed to the bed and wrenched a metal bar from the frame. It was an easy thing for a man of his strength to accomplish.

64
00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:56.866
"I advise you not to disturb me now," said Valjean quietly.

65
00:05:56.867 --> 00:06:06.104
Javert stood by the door while Valjean knelt next to Fantine’s bed. He whispered something to her, took her hand, and gently kissed it.

66
00:06:06.105 --> 00:06:10.878
Valjean stood up and said to Javert, "Now I am free to leave with you."

67
00:06:10.879 --> 00:06:14.866
The mayor’s arrest produced a sensation in the town.

68
00:06:14.867 --> 00:06:22.533
In less than two hours, his good deeds were forgotten as everyone discussed the convict in their midst.

69
00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:29.025
That night Valjean’s housekeeper was thinking sadly about the mayor when he suddenly walked in the door.

70
00:06:29.026 --> 00:06:31.971
"Monsieur Mayor! I thought you were—"

71
00:06:31.972 --> 00:06:39.763
"In jail? I broke a bar from a window, jumped from a roof, and here I am. Find Sister Simplice for me. It’s urgent!"

72
00:06:39.764 --> 00:06:45.993
Valjean went up to his room. He quickly wrapped up the silver candlesticks and packed them with some other things.

73
00:06:45.994 --> 00:06:51.850
"Do you wish to see Fantine’s body one last time?" asked Sister Simplice when she arrived.

74
00:06:51.851 --> 00:06:57.326
"No, I’m leaving some money here for her burial. Make sure the priest gets it."

75
00:06:57.327 --> 00:07:01.160
At that moment there was the sound of voices downstairs.

76
00:07:01.161 --> 00:07:05.747
"I swear that no one has come in here all day," said the housekeeper.

77
00:07:05.748 --> 00:07:08.600
"But there’s a light upstairs," said Javert.

78
00:07:08.601 --> 00:07:11.898
Valjean blew out his candle and hid behind the door.

79
00:07:11.899 --> 00:07:18.470
When Javert burst through the door, Sister Simplice was kneeling in prayer by the light of one small candle.

80
00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:28.137
Javert hesitated. He had great respect for authority and especially for the church, so he didn’t want to disturb a nun at prayer. And yet. . .

81
00:07:28.138 --> 00:07:34.541
"Sister, Valjean has escaped and we’re looking for him. Have you seen him?"

82
00:07:34.542 --> 00:07:38.121
Sister Simplice raised her eyes. "No."

83
00:07:38.122 --> 00:07:46.462
An hour later a man carrying a bundle walked rapidly out of town, headed in the direction of Paris.

